; Finalize's Phase 3 prices a conversion between two lots of one
; commodity with a cost in that same commodity: it balances the
; transaction but is not a basis.  When the lot prices are in different
; commodities, Phase 6 cannot restate that cost in a common currency,
; so --basis must read the lot's annotation price (EUR700), not the
; balancing conversion (10 AAPL {$70}).  When both lot prices share a
; currency, Phase 6 restates the cost in it (EUR-700 / EUR700).

2024/01/15 * Buy stock
    Assets:Brokerage       10 AAPL {$70.00}
    Assets:Checking              $-700.00

2024/06/01 * Re-denominate lot
    Assets:Brokerage      -10 AAPL {$70.00}
    Assets:Brokerage       20 AAPL {35.00 EUR}

2024/07/01 * Two-for-one split
    Assets:Brokerage      -20 AAPL {35.00 EUR}
    Assets:Brokerage       40 AAPL {17.50 EUR}

test reg --basis --columns=80 Brokerage
24-Jan-15 Buy stock             Assets:Brokerage            $700.00      $700.00
24-Jun-01 Re-denominate lot     Assets:Brokerage           $-700.00            0
                                Assets:Brokerage             EUR700       EUR700
24-Jul-01 Two-for-one split     Assets:Brokerage            EUR-700            0
                                Assets:Brokerage             EUR700       EUR700
end test

test bal --basis --columns=80
            $-700.00
              EUR700  Assets
              EUR700    Brokerage
            $-700.00    Checking
--------------------
            $-700.00
              EUR700
end test
